Compile the synchronize checklist's Explorer file operation on Windows only.

TSynchronizeChecklistFileOperation carries out a synchronization checklist
through Explorer's IFileOperation (a Shell COM object), so that local
deletions go to the recycle bin with Explorer's progress and undo. Only
WinSCP's Windows GUI uses it (CustomScpExplorer.cpp). Elsewhere neither the
object nor the interfaces exist, and declaring them only to compile would
pretend to a facility that is not there; a frontend on another platform
implements the operation its own way. The class and its implementation are
guarded with _WIN32, which C++Builder defines, so upstream's build is
unchanged. Each guard replaces a separator comment line, so line counts are
unchanged.

